! POWHEG-RES, muon NC DIS on the FASERnu MUON FLUX -- the setup of
! arXiv:2506.13889 (Francener, Goncalves, Kling, Krack, Rojo), reproduced
! here as a check of the benchmark's event-rate machinery (user, 2026-09-03).
!
! WHAT DIFFERS FROM THE BENCHMARK CARDS, AND WHY EACH IS DELIBERATE:
!   fixed_lepton_beam 0 + LEPpdf 111222334
!       the incoming muon is drawn from the FLUX (an LHAPDF grid, index
!       111222334 = mu- + mu+ summed, data/faser_muon_flux/lhapdf/), so the
!       integrated "cross-section" POWHEG reports is already a NUMBER OF
!       EVENTS at 250 fb^-1 on 50 cm of tungsten nucleons (the flux is
!       normalised as n_T L_T dN/dx in pb^-1, Eq. 2.1 of the paper).
!   ebeam1 7000d0   the paper's own card (DIS/testrun/powheg.input-save in
!       LHCfitNikhef/DIS_with_LHC_muons); the muon energy is x * ebeam1.
!       The grid's x is defined with sqrt(s_pp) = 13.6 TeV, i.e. E = 6800 x,
!       so 7000 puts every muon 2.9% high -- kept, because the point is to
!       reproduce THEIR number, and stated.
!   Qmin 1.65d0     the paper's DIS cut Q > 1.65 GeV, applied at generation as
!       in their card (the leptonic Q is untouched by QCD radiation).
!   alphaem 1/137, s2w 1-(mW/mZ)^2 = 0.22265   THEIR electroweak point -- their
!       card sets neither, so the code defaults apply.  The benchmark's Gmu
!       point (1/132.119) would raise a photon-exchange rate by (137/132.119)^2
!       = 7.5%, which is the single largest convention difference between the
!       two setups.
!   ymin 0 / ymax 1  no y window (theirs has none); the target is a PROTON
!       (ih2 1), as in their card, not the (Z p + N n)/A nucleon of the text.
! Everything else -- NNPDF4.0 NNLO, muF = muR = Q, NLO+PS with the same
! POWHEG-RES binary -- is common to both.

numevts 50000        ! events per seed; 8 seeds -> 400k total

ih1 13               ! lepton beam: mu-
ih2  1               ! hadron 2 (1 for protons)
ebeam1 7000d0        ! x * ebeam1 = muon energy; the paper's card (see header)
ebeam2 0.938d0       ! proton at rest (mass)
fixed_lepton_beam 0  ! lepton drawn from the flux grid below
LEPpdf 111222334     ! data/faser_muon_flux/lhapdf/muon_flux_FASERv_Run3_var2_sum, read by the paper's lepton_flux.f
fixed_target 1       ! beam 2 at rest, mass = ebeam2

bornktmin 0d0
bornsuppfact 0d0     ! no Born suppression: flat event weights

Qmin 1.65d0          ! the paper's DIS cut Q > 1.65 GeV, at generation as in their card
Qmax 100000d0
xmin 0d0
xmax 1d0
ymin 0d0
ymax 1d0

lhans1   331100      ! NNPDF40_nnlo_as_01180
lhans2   331100
alphas_from_pdf 1

renscfact  1d0
facscfact  1d0
runningscales 1      ! muF = muR = Q

channel_type 4       ! NC only
vtype 3              ! photon + Z exchange
smartsig 1
nores 1
olddij 0

! EW parameters: Gmu-scheme values used as fixed couplings (matched to Sherpa)
alphaem 0.0072992700729927d0   ! 1/137, THEIR default (see header)
s2w 0.22265d0        ! 1 - (80.398/91.1876)^2, THEIR default

muonmass 0.10566d0

use-old-grid    1
use-old-ubound  1

ncall1 50000         ! calls per process for importance-sampling grid
itmx1 1              ! (xgriditerations handled by parallel stage 1)
ncall2 50000         ! calls per process for upper-bounding envelope
itmx2 1
foldcsi 5
foldy   5
foldphi 1
nubound 50000
iupperfsr 1

fastbtlbound 1
storemintupb 1
ubexcess_correct 1
storeinfo_rwgt 1
hdamp 0
bornzerodamp 1

withnegweights 1
flg_jacsing 1
testplots 0

xupbound 2d0
iseed    12
manyseeds 1
doublefsr 0

parallelstage 4
xgriditeration 1
